From tru64-unix-managers  Fri Nov 19 07:31:29 1999
From: Nikola Milutinovic <Nikola.Milutinovic () ev ! co ! yu>
Date: Fri, 19 Nov 1999 07:31:29 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: NFS over TCP
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079085416306

OK, here's the answer.

Digital UNIX 3.2G and prior to that does not support NFS over TCP (my case).
Digital UNIX 4.0D does support it and happily works with it. I suppose versions
A and B/C do as well.

What I overlooked in my test case is that, on my 4.0D machine, I forgot to setup
the NFS at all. So it seamed to me that DU doesn't support it at all. Now that
is cleared. Thanks to all who responded.

Nix.

From tru64-unix-managers  Thu Nov 18 23:57:46 1999
