From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Nov 17 22:13:39 1999
From: "Spalding, Stephen" <SSpaldin () mem-ins ! com>
Date: Wed, 17 Nov 1999 22:13:39 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Sendmail problem after 4.0F upgrade
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079085416280

My original question was:

"I just upgraded my Alpha Server 2100 to Tru64 UNIX 4.0F, and one of the
> problems that I have run into deals with mail. I understand that 4.0F
> upgrades you to version 8.8.8 of sendmail which is quite a ways ahead of
> where we were at. The problem that I'm having is when ever I send an email
> from the Alpha Server, I get a message displayed back to the screen that
> says "NIS map mail.aliases specified, but NIS not running". I am still
> very
> new to sendmail, so I'm not certain where the problem is at. I have looked
> through sendmail.cf and do not see any reference to mail.aliases. Can
> anyone
> point me in the right direction?"
> 
> 
Sean O'Connell responded right away and hit the nail on the head. He
instructed me to look in /etc/svc.conf and make sure that there are no
references to yp. When I looked in the file, yp was on every line. I removed
each reference to yp and now mail does go out of the Alpha Server.

I messed with NIS and yp earlier in the year but decided not to do anything
with it at this time. I thought that I had cleaned it up, but apparently I
did not manage to do so.

Thanks Sean!

-Stephen Spalding

