PROBLEM1:

daemon.log:
Nov 11 19:05:44 EDSO [400]:  **ERROR svrsys_fru_parse.c line 1031: FRU Table
revision 2.0 is not supported

SOLUTION1:

FRU is "Field Replaceable Unit", a table formatted by the firmware upon boot.
Kernel expects a certain version of it and the firmware on my older machine is
outdated, as it seams. Firmware upgrade is suggested and I'll do it, ASAP.

------
PROBLEM2:

daemon.log:

Nov  8 19:24:38 EDRU [404]: Initializing the thresold structure 
Nov  8 19:24:38 EDRU [404]:  WARNING svrMgt_persist.c line 364: error m
opening /etc/thresholds.dat
Nov  8 19:24:38 EDRU [404]:  WARNING svrMgt_persist.c line 127: error m
linking /etc/thresholds.dat and /etc/thresholds.dat.bak

SOLUTION2:

This seams to be a minor bug in SNMP. "touch /etc/thresholds.dat" should solve
it.

------
PROBLEM3:

daemon.log:
Nov  9 09:46:54 EDRU telnetd[4637]: ttloop:  peer died: Error 0 occurred

SOLUTION3:

Could be due to misconfigured NIC. Like I said, high loads and bad (NE2000) NIC
in DOS mode are a known source of troubles.

