New Subscriber - Basic Question - Got the answer

The process I was using submits a job using Batch - this in return submits a
job to "at" using the following format "at -qb -m". This is held in /usr/bin
in a file batch. By removing the -m option you will only receive
notifications if there are problems.


>>>>>Environment - Digitial Unix V4.0d

>>>>>When I use cron to submit jobs I get a message to say that the job has
completed. How do I remove this default notification?

>>>>>If I use the MAN pages it implies that the -M switch will mail a job
successful message, therefore this flag must also be the current default,
how do I change this?



Many thanks for all suggestions received.

Tony McCormack

