Content-Type: text/plain

A basic question for those who know syslog well:
AS1200
4.0D

I am seeing a local network app writing to the NSR log in:
"/nsr/logs/summary"

I have an entry in /etc/syslog.conf for logging of the local app as follows:

local0.warning	/var/log/myapp.log

Within the NSR created section of the syslog.conf I have:

# %BRX421_BEGIN% - DO NOT MODIFY OR DELETE(date)
daemon.notice	/dev/console
daemon.notice	/nsr/logs/messages
daemon.notice	operator
local0.notice	/nsr/logs/summary
local0.alert	root, operator
# %BRX421_END% - DO NOT MODIFY OR DELETE

Is the local app sending it's logging info to "local0" and
conflicting with the NSR logging to local0 as well ?

Should the local app be changed to send logging to local[1-7] ?


***********************
Wayne Sweatt
Principal Software Analyst
Litton / PRC
505.827.9288
